# Pairs with RAllOrNothing, and reproduces issue #4480 as production had it
# before ReplicationShipperGrain's terminal hold: the transport may deliver a
# source shard's terminal before that shard's prepare. The receiver's tally
# completes, its leaf applies the commit with no bucket to drain - recording
# the terminal and materialising nothing - and one key is served post-saga while
# the other is still pre-saga. Before #4510 the prepare that arrived next was
# refused as late and the split was permanent; the receiver's settle now
# materialises it under the committed registry, so the split is transient, which
# this state invariant still reports.
#
# The shipper merged WAL partitions by HLC within one pump tick only, and HLCs
# are not monotonic in a partition's append order, so a terminal could ship
# ahead of a prepare of its own saga. The hold now keeps every terminal back
# until the peer has acknowledged every prepare of its saga; with it switched
# off (TerminalHoldsRequired false) the shipper's ordering detectors go red, and
# the end-to-end skewed-log detector goes red once the settle is switched off
# too. That is this mutation's production analogue.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingTerminalOvertakesPrepare
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a source shard's terminal may be delivered before that shard's prepare, which the receiver then refuses
PERTURBS: DeliverTerminal

--- FIND
    /\ \A p \in outbox : (p.type = "prep" /\ p.key = m.key) => p \in dlv
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no per-shard ordering; any terminal may overtake its prepare.
    /\ TRUE
--- END
